Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.00,0:00:12.99,Default,,0,0,0,,What if I told you that Lord Shiva once\Nfaced an enemy he could not destroy?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.79,0:00:22.40,Default,,0,0,0,,An entity so powerful, so invincible, that the combined\Nforces of the cosmos were brought to their knees.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.85,0:00:26.64,Default,,0,0,0,,But the greatest mystery isn't how strong this demon was...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.09,0:00:28.96,Default,,0,0,0,,it’s where he came from.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.41,0:00:32.53,Default,,0,0,0,,To defeat him, the Gods couldn't use weapons.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.98,0:00:37.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Lord Vishnu had to commit the ultimate sin of betrayal.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.02,0:00:43.46,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the forgotten legend of Jalandhara—the\Ndemon who wore the face of a God.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.66,0:00:48.46,Default,,0,0,0,,The story begins not with evil, but with arrogance.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.91,0:00:57.19,Default,,0,0,0,,When Indra, the King of the Gods, dared to challenge Lord\NShiva, Shiva's third eye opened in apocalyptic fury.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.64,0:01:04.98,Default,,0,0,0,,To save the universe from immediate destruction, the fire\Nwas diverted and thrown into the depths of the ocean.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.43,0:01:09.08,Default,,0,0,0,,But the energy of the destroyer does not simply vanish.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.53,0:01:13.22,Default,,0,0,0,,From the boiling waters of the sea, a child was born.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.67,0:01:25.36,Default,,0,0,0,,His name was Jalandhara—literally meaning "He who holds the water." Born from Shiva’s pure\Nwrath, he was destined to be the most terrifying force the three worlds had ever seen.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.56,0:01:31.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Jalandhara grew into an unstoppable emperor of the Asuras.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.29,0:01:37.86,Default,,0,0,0,,But his true power wasn't just his brute strength\Nit was a closely guarded secret.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.31,0:01:40.32,Default,,0,0,0,,It was his wife, Vrinda.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.77,0:01:46.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Vrinda was a woman of unmatched purity and\Nan absolute devotee of Lord Vishnu.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.25,0:01:53.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Her devotion and loyalty created a mystical\Nimpenetrable shield around her husband.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.99,0:02:01.16,Default,,0,0,0,,As long as Vrinda remained faithful and her chastity\Nwas unbroken, Jalandhara was literally immortal.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.16,0:02:06.91,Default,,0,0,0,,No weapon forged in the cosmos could\Nleave a single scratch on his skin.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.11,0:02:11.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Drunk on power, Jalandhara did the unthinkable.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.69,0:02:21.31,Default,,0,0,0,,He dethroned Indra, conquered the heavens, and finally, marched\Non Mount Kailash to challenge his own creator—Lord Shiva.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.76,0:02:23.70,Default,,0,0,0,,The battle was catastrophic.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.15,0:02:29.77,Default,,0,0,0,,The universe shook as the Creator of Destruction\Nfought the byproduct of his own anger.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.22,0:02:35.21,Default,,0,0,0,,But as Shiva's Trishul struck Jalandhara\Nthe Gods watched in pure horror.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.21,0:02:38.08,Default,,0,0,0,,The weapon bounced off.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.53,0:02:44.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Because of Vrinda's spiritual shield, even\Nthe Supreme Destroyer could not kill him.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.52,0:02:48.05,Default,,0,0,0,,The cosmos was on the brink of total annihilation.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.25,0:02:50.93,Default,,0,0,0,,The Gods were desperate.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.38,0:02:56.71,Default,,0,0,0,,There was only one way to end the war, and\Nit required a sacrifice of morality.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.16,0:03:03.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Lord Vishnu, the preserver of the universe, had to\Nmake a heartbreaking choice to save existence.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.38,0:03:11.24,Default,,0,0,0,,While Jalandhara fought Shiva, Vishnu disguised himself\Nas the demon king and appeared before Vrinda.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.24,0:03:16.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Believing him to be her victorious\Nhusband, she embraced him.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.75,0:03:24.93,Default,,0,0,0,,In that single, fleeting moment, the illusion was complete—and\Nher vow of absolute fidelity was technically broken.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.13,0:03:31.05,Default,,0,0,0,,The moment the deception occurred, Jalandhara’s\Ninvincible shield shattered.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.05,0:03:39.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Miles away on the battlefield, Shiva’s trident finally\Npierced the demon's heart, ending his reign of terror.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.70,0:03:41.89,Default,,0,0,0,,But the tragedy was just beginning.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.34,0:03:49.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Realizing she had been tricked by the very God she\Nworshipped, Vrinda was consumed by grief and fury.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.91,0:03:57.38,Default,,0,0,0,,She cursed Lord Vishnu, declaring that because he acted\Nlike a heartless stone, he would be turned into one.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.58,0:04:05.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Vishnu accepted her curse with bowed head, transforming\Nhis aspect into the black Shaligram stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.35,0:04:13.40,Default,,0,0,0,,And from the ashes of the tragic Vrinda grew a plant\Nthat would become sacred to all of India—the Tulsi.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.40,0:04:25.78,Default,,0,0,0,,To this day, the Shaligram and the Tulsi are worshipped together, forever bound\Nby a story of cosmic war, divine duty, and a betrayal that saved the universe.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.78,0:04:31.34,Default,,0,0,0,,If you seek more hidden mysteries from\Nthe ancient texts, hit subscribe.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.79,0:04:34.62,Default,,0,0,0,,The legends of Bharath are deeper than you know.
